Later that same evening, I am at home in my apartment.
Nina knocks on my door.
We are going down to the water to see the bonfire.
She comes inside and looks at my small backpack.
"Have you packed a warm jacket for tonight?" she asks.
I nod and open the bag.
"Yes, I have put my thickest sweater in here," I answer.
"The wind blew strongly earlier in the afternoon."
"So the air suddenly became a bit cold," I add.
Nina smiles and looks out of the window.
"That was a good idea," she says.
"The sun has shone all day."
"But it often gets chilly by the water."
I put on my shoes and take my keys.
I bought the sweater in January when I moved to Denmark.
It has been a wonderful birthday, and I am not tired at all.
We go out into the hallway, and I lock the door behind us.
I am completely ready for the evening at the beach.
